ayload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"cd82cd163ecf50011436966f805333cb8978ae8633bdcb9cb57f86aaf8b00468","event_uuid":"0aece67a-21eb-4cd6-8e48-342e94e28c92","position":{"commit_sha":"6f5027f1840d9a1c1e6a7538c8a5a46a6d9ce6da","position":"1785450637497405001-0aece67a-21eb-4cd6-8e48-342e94e28c92"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e851d701c2eea59de46fadf6c6b29259a0bf62bb7ab73393151f27be15afe567","event_uuid":"8a74c32f-9708-41c6-93dd-3d92ae05de0b","position":{"commit_sha":"6f5027f1840d9a1c1e6a7538c8a5a46a6d9ce6da","position":"1785450638193986001-8a74c32f-9708-41c6-93dd-3d92ae05de0b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"03a7b3fb99378ea582a6a3581218e7db25b06188a4fe50458cc21c640b3b078b","event_uuid":"d3a5803c-3f4e-46ee-8e69-f199ba3e221d","position":{"commit_sha":"3f579f286617bec9d09667daa2a95f8d6782d937","position":"1785451133708291395-d3a5803c-3f4e-46ee-8e69-f199ba3e221d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"b707f729-f629-4867-9965-f2ea0e303433","comments":[],"created_at":1785444513426747001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9ad58ab5-cc54-4868-aa16-0d41f06dc666","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2132-e48f-425c-4f24"},{"link_uuid":"cfe150b7-8c7b-4cb9-8495-68a746876f41","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9664-784b-c5ec-4089"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nA single Gerrit Verified run needs 21 concurrent job slots. The navapbc org is on GitHub Free: 20 total concurrent jobs and 5 concurrent macOS, enforced PER ORGANIZATION and shared with every other navapbc repo. So one run, in an otherwise idle org, cannot fully parallelize; under a 6-change burst later runs queued 6.7-8.4m for a macOS slot, which is what turns a ~21m run into the 41-47m seen from Gerrit.\n\n`.github/workflows/_optionality.yml` fans out 5 `per-extra` matrix cells plus a `union` cell — 6 jobs, each doing 0.4-0.8m of real work while holding a slot for a full checkout + setup-python + install.\n\n(The redundant `import-linter` job is handled separately in ticket 2132-e48f-425c-4f24; this ticket does not touch it.)\n\n## Approach\nCollapse the 5 `per-extra` cells + `union` into ONE job running a venv loop.\n\nITERATIONS. Five-plus-one is WRONG as originally drafted, because the current matrix list and `_optional.EXTRAS` are not the same set. Verified: `_optional.EXTRAS == {agents, eval, grounding, metrics, tracing}` while the matrix runs `{agents, eval, tracing, mcp, grounding}`. So:\n- `mcp` is NOT in `_optional.EXTRAS` — it is the server transport, has no detection probe, and is validated by its boot check instead.\n- `metrics` IS in `_optional.EXTRAS` and has NO per-extra CI today — a real pre-existing gap the loop closes for free.\nThe loop therefore runs over `_optional.EXTRAS` keys UNION `{mcp}` = six isolation iterations, PLUS one UNION iteration installing `.[agents,eval,tracing]` jointly into a single venv. The union is not redundant with the isolation runs: it is the only thing exercising JOINT dependency resolution and can surface a `ResolutionImpossible` no single-extra install can.\n\nPER-ITERATION WORK must reproduce everything the current cells do, not just the install:\n- `import rebar` with the extra present;\n- for extras in `_optional.EXTRAS`, assert `_optional.extra_installed(extra)` (the detection probe);\n- `rebar-mcp --help` for the mcp iteration ONLY, reproducing today's `if: matrix.extra == 'mcp'`. Running it everywhere fails in venvs lacking the entry point; dropping it silently weakens the mcp boot check.\n\nTWO ABSOLUTE RULES, each guarding a silent-failure mode:\n- NEVER `source .../activate`. Activations STACK across iterations, so PATH decides which interpreter runs and every iteration can silently re-test extra #1.\n- ALWAYS invoke by absolute path (`\"$v/bin/python\"`, `\"$v/bin/rebar-mcp\"`). A bare `python`/`rebar-mcp` runs the AMBIENT interpreter and can pass while testing nothing. Today's `rebar-mcp --help` (_optionality.yml:178-180) is exactly such a bare console-script call and must be rewritten.\n\nERROR ISOLATION is explicit because Actions runs `run:` under `bash -e`: a naive loop dies on the first failure (losing today's `fail-fast: false` diagnostics), while `|| true`/`set +e` without aggregation makes the whole contract a no-op that ALWAYS PASSES. Use an `rc` accumulator — guard each iteration with `|| { rc=1; echo \"::error::<extra> failed\"; continue; }` and end the step with `exit $rc`.\n\nVENV HYGIENE: `python -m venv` from a `setup-python` interpreter is already clean (user site-packages disabled, `include-system-site-packages=false`), and `PYTHONPATH`/`PIP_*` are unset in both workflows, so `--copies`/`PYTHONNOUSERSITE`/`--without-pip` are NOT needed. The pip HTTP cache shared across venvs is a speed benefit only (wheels are content-addressed). Run `pip install --upgrade pip` per venv (ensurepip ships an old pip).\n\nKEEP `clean-core-wheel` byte-identical. It is the check this file header credits with catching \"the module-scope-import class that escaped once\", it builds a real wheel, and it is the ONLY lane where `agents_extra_installed()` is False — which is what makes its skipif-degradation tests actually execute.\n\nRejected: sequential `pip install .[agents]` then `.[eval]` into one shared python — after the first install the env is contaminated, so a missing dependency declaration in a later extra PASSES silently; that is the exact bug class this workflow exists to catch. Rejected: per-extra venvs with no union iteration (loses joint resolution). Rejected: collapsing `clean-core-wheel` in. Considered and not chosen: `strategy: {max-parallel: 1}` on the existing matrix (5->1 peak slots, zero new bash) — the loop was chosen deliberately for the larger slot saving.\n\n## Scope\n- `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml` — replace the `per-extra` matrix job and the `union` job with the single venv-loop job.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` — durable guards on the loop shape and extras coverage.\n- `infra/github/main-protection.snapshot.json` — it hard-codes the doomed check names (`extra \"agents\" installs`, `union [agents,eval,tracing] resolves`, ...). It is not the live ruleset (that is Terraform `gerrit-mirror-lock-main`, which declares no `required_status_checks`), but it IS POSTed back by `infra/github/rollback-mirror-lock.sh:75-88` — so leaving it stale means an emergency rollback would demand checks that cannot exist and would freeze `main`.\n\nNOT in scope: `import-linter` (ticket 2132), `clean-core-wheel`, `_build-and-test.yml`, `gerrit-verify.yaml`.\n\n## Testing\nDurable checked-in guards, not one-time manual observations, because the risk is a later careless edit:\n- assert the loop step text contains the `rc` accumulator shape (`continue` and `exit $rc`) and contains NO `activate`, so the swallowed-failure and stacked-activation footguns cannot be reintroduced silently;\n- assert every key in `_optional.EXTRAS` appears in the looped extra list, so a newly declared extra cannot ship with zero CI.\n\nWorkflow-level validation: `optionality.yml` triggers on `push`, so pushing a scratch branch to the GitHub mirror exercises the modified reusable end-to-end. A PULL REQUEST does NOT work — `.github/workflows/lockdown.yml` runs `dessant/repo-lockdown` on `pull_request_target` with `close-pr: true` (only dependabot exempt), so the mirror auto-closes PRs. `workflow_dispatch` on `optionality.yml` is the fallback.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each isolation extra installs into its own freshly-created venv, never one that already had another extra installed.\n- [ ] The isolation iteration set equals `_optional.EXTRAS` keys plus `mcp`, so `metrics` gains per-extra CI it does not have today.\n- [ ] A UNION iteration installs `.[agents,eval,tracing]` jointly into one venv.\n- [ ] Each isolation iteration runs `import rebar` and, for extras in `_optional.EXTRAS`, asserts `_optional.extra_installed(extra)`.\n- [ ] `rebar-mcp --help` runs for the mcp iteration only, invoked by absolute venv path.\n- [ ] Every interpreter/console-script call in the loop uses an absolute `\"$v/bin/...\"` path, and the loop contains no `activate`.\n- [ ] The loop uses an `rc` accumulator with `continue` and exits non-zero if any iteration failed.\n- [ ] A checked-in test asserts the loop step contains `exit $rc` and `continue` and no `activate`.\n- [ ] A checked-in test asserts the looped extra list covers every key in `_optional.EXTRAS`.\n- [ ] `clean-core-wheel` is byte-identical to its current form.\n- [ ] `infra/github/main-protection.snapshot.json` no longer names removed checks.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` and `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` pass.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes (actionlint covers all workflows).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/_optionality.yml","reason":"delete import-linter; replace per-extra matrix + union with six-iteration venv loop"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","reason":"durable guards: 9-test collection, loop shape, extras-vs-_optional.EXTRAS parity"},{"path":"infra/github/main-protection.snapshot.json","reason":"drop removed check names so an emergency rollback cannot freeze main"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2132-e48f-425c-4f24"],["relates_to","9664-784b-c5ec-4089"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"0aece67a-21eb-4cd6-8e48-342e94e28c92","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ad63-17ad-d545-45d4","ticket_type":"task","title":"Collapse the optionality per-extra fan-out into one venv-per-extra job","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["68f90ec4-6577-4c53-9ac9-901d2497c885","b57660cd-53c1-48b2-8191-391b764ebac9","5122e695-81db-4b20-bb97-c24154e5b168","49dc7e99-a85f-48b4-88ba-4857f6eea9c9","4b744535-38d3-44f0-abd3-34d27d50d590","9b48d21a-2ab4-4a2b-bc59-d7367d21d5e2","9ad58ab5-cc54-4868-aa16-0d41f06dc666","76d201f9-0981-49d6-bd7d-e7c5275e3ef5","0aece67a-21eb-4cd6-8e48-342e94e28c92","8a74c32f-9708-41c6-93dd-3d92ae05de0b","d3a5803c-3f4e-46ee-8e69-f199ba3e221d","cfe150b7-8c7b-4cb9-8495-68a746876f41"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785453310648300390,"uuid":"b0129ae3-9782-4602-a39e-490dae3fda65"}